    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "p0",
        "title": "RG Is a Choice, Not a Reflex",
        "text": "The strategy guide's rule of thumb: counter attack after RGing C normals and SPECIALS, after some B normals - and if you RG an A or 2A, JUST KEEP BLOCKING. Fast normals cancel into the next hit before your punish comes out; you lose that race every time."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "The Perfect RG Targets",
        "text": "Dash normals and specials are the jackpot. Makoto's {input:66B} is +2 on normal block - but on Recoil Guard she has 10 frames of raw recovery and nothing cheap to cancel into. That is a free punish window of over 7 frames. Specials are even worse for her: RG turns 20+ frames of blockstun into almost nothing."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "title": "When NOT to RG",
        "text": "Some moves are so unsafe on normal block that RG only gives the attacker a chance to counter-RG your punish. If the move already loses hard on block - just block it and take the guaranteed punish."
      }
    ],
